Chain: Bugfix

Purpose:
  The stage sequence for resolving a defect in existing functionality.
  AN/QA/VR are not redefined here — see templates/feature.sdd -> Stages
  for the same names, same meaning (see NoDuplication).

Sequence:
  AN -> IMPACT -> FIX -> QA -> VR

Stages:

  AN  -> see templates/feature.sdd -> Stages -> AN (same name, same
    meaning)

  IMPACT: Impact Analysis
    meaning: Determine which layers (API/BE/DB/FE/MD) the bug's visible
      symptom actually touches, before FIX begins — the visible symptom
      and its real impact surface are not the same thing (see
      chains.sdd -> Stages -> chain-orchestration stages).

  FIX: Fix Implementation
    meaning: The corrective change itself, scoped strictly to what
      IMPACT identified — touching a layer IMPACT did not flag is out
      of scope for this stage (see Rules [BF2] below).

  QA  -> @../stages/QA.sdd
  VR  -> @../stages/VR.sdd

Rules:
  [BF1] IMPACT MUST complete before FIX begins (see chains.sdd -> Rules
        [C5]). Example: a report of "payment error in the mobile app"
        MUST NOT go straight to FIX — IMPACT MUST first determine which
        of the API/BE/DB/FE/MD layers are actually involved, otherwise
        the visible symptom gets patched while the root cause remains.
  [BF2] FIX MUST NOT change a layer outside the scope IMPACT identified
        — a "no silent expansion" counterpart to chains.sdd -> Rules
        [C7]'s "no silent skip".

State: +

Note:
  (prompt/new/33.md, STEP 11) Supersedes ../bugfix.chain (STEP 5),
  deleted in this same pass (preserved in git history).

  Distinguished from templates/change.sdd: bugfix does not change the
  architecture, it restores previously-declared behavior; if the
  behavior itself must change, see templates/change.sdd.

  QA/VR now point at ./../stages/*.sdd instead of being assumed by name
  only (old bugfix.chain listed them in Sequence but never pointed
  anywhere) — same NoDuplication fix applied to templates/feature.sdd.

  Content translated from the original Azerbaijani (old bugfix.chain)
  into English, per the standing "apply, don't copy" rule.
